B.b6r=new A.mI("What is this app?","The AW139 Power Assurance Calculator helps you verify that your AW139 helicopter engines are producing sufficient power under current environmental conditions, in accordance with the Flight Manual power assurance check procedure.",null)
B.b6G=new A.mI("1 \u2014 Select Configuration","Choose the rotor speed (NR) and inlet filter type that matches your aircraft configuration:\n\u2022 NR 100% or 102%\n\u2022 EAPS (Engine Air Particle Separator)\n\u2022 IBF (Inlet Barrier Filter)\n\u2022 No filter (clean intake)",null)
B.b6p=new A.mI("2 \u2014 Enter Environmental Data","Fill in the current conditions at the time of the check:\n\u2022 Elevation (ft) \u2014 pressure altitude of the airfield\n\u2022 Torque (%) \u2014 torque set for the check\n\u2022 OAT (\xb0C) \u2014 outside air temperature",null)
B.b6w=new A.mI("3 \u2014 Enter Engine Readings","Record the aircraft registration and the steady-state readings for each engine:\n\u2022 NG (%) \u2014 gas generator speed\n\u2022 ITT (\xb0C) \u2014 inter-turbine temperature",null)
B.b6F=new A.mI("4 \u2014 Read the Results","The calculator displays the limits (Max NG and Max ITT) interpolated from the Flight Manual tables for your conditions.\n\nEach engine reading is compared against the limit:\n\u2022 Green \u25bc \u2014 engine is below the limit (pass)\n\u2022 Red \u25b2 \u2014 engine exceeds the limit (fail)\n\nThe delta value shows the margin to the limit.",null)
B.b6z=new A.mI("5 \u2014 Save & Export","Tap Save to store the check in the history log.\nTap PDF to generate and share a printable report.\nThe history log keeps your last checks for reference.\nSwipe a history entry left to delete it individually.",null)
B.b6E=new A.mI("Graph","Tap the graph preview in the results card to open a full-screen overlay showing your operating point plotted on the Flight Manual performance chart.",null)
B.aJA=s([B.b6r,B.b6G,B.b6p,B.b6w,B.b6F,B.b6z,B.b6E],t.p)
B.W1=new A.iT(B.aN,B.K,B.br,B.ai,null,B.W,null,0,B.aJA,null)
B.aXp=new A.ms(null,B.W1,null)
B.b6D=new A.mH("What is this tool?","This calculator determines if the AW139 bleed valve closing point is within the acceptable NG range for the current temperature, and calculates any adjustment required.",null)
B.b6m=new A.mH("1 \u2014 Enter Temperature","Enter the ambient temperature in \xb0C at the time of the check. Valid range: -50 to 50 \xb0C.\n\nTip: use the mouse scroll wheel on the field to increment/decrement by 1 \xb0C.",null)
B.b6C=new A.mH("2 \u2014 Enter Engine NG","Enter the NG (%) at which the bleed valve closed during the engine run. Valid range: 78.5 to 94.3 %.\n\nTip: scroll wheel changes the value by 0.1 % increments.",null)
B.b6B=new A.mH("3 \u2014 Read the Chart","The chart shows the acceptable range between the red and green curves:\n\u2022 Red curve \u2014 minimum acceptable NG\n\u2022 Green curve \u2014 maximum acceptable NG\n\u2022 Blue vertical line \u2014 current temperature\n\u2022 Blue horizontal line \u2014 current NG reading\n\nTap the chart to open a full-screen zoomable view.",null)
B.b6s=new A.mH("4 \u2014 Read the Result","If the NG is within the band: no adjustment needed.\n\nIf outside:\n\u2022 NG too HIGH (closes too late) \u2192 CCW adjustment\n\u2022 NG too LOW (closes too early) \u2192 CW adjustment\n\n1 flat \u2248 1.3% NG change. Maximum 2 flats per adjustment.",null)
B.b6v=new A.mH("5 \u2014 Share PDF","Once a valid temperature is entered, a share button appears. Tap it to generate and share a PDF report with the chart and adjustment instructions.",null)
B.b6n=new A.mH("Safety","Always refer to up-to-date official AW139 maintenance publications before performing any adjustment. This tool is for reference only.",null)
